  "title": "Review: hello & goodbye",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Put Unit 1 together into a full mini-conversation:\n\n- **আসসালামু আলাইকুম।** — **ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম।**\n- **কেমন আছেন?** — **ভালো আছি, আর আপনি?**\n- **আপনার নাম কী?** — **আমার নাম রাফি।**\n- **খোদা হাফেজ!** — **আবার দেখা হবে।**\n\n**খোদা হাফেজ** (*khoda hafez*, 'may God protect you') is the usual goodbye in Bangladesh; **আল্লাহ হাফেজ** (*allah hafez*) is also common. Hindu speakers and people in Kolkata often say **আসি** (*ashi*, lit. 'I'll come [again]') or **আবার দেখা হবে**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "khoda-hafez",
      "bn": "খোদা হাফেজ",
      "tr": "khoda hafez",
      "en": "goodbye",
      "notes": "Lit. 'may God protect you'. Variant: আল্লাহ হাফেজ (allah hafez). The z sound in hafez comes from Arabic; many speakers say 'hafej'."
    },
    {
      "id": "abar-dekha-hobe",
      "bn": "আবার দেখা হবে",
      "tr": "abar dekha hobe",
      "en": "see you again",
      "notes": "Lit. 'there will be a meeting again'. Neutral, used by everyone in both Bangladesh and West Bengal."
    }
  ],
